# Pin this project to the public npm registry.
#
# Without this, whatever `registry` is set globally on the machine wins, and its
# host gets baked into package-lock.json's `resolved` URLs. A work Artifactory
# leaked in that way twice here: it published an internal hostname to this
# public repo, and it broke every build without credentials for that registry
# (the Vercel deploy failed on `npm install` with E401).
#
# No credentials belong in this file. Auth stays in ~/.npmrc, which is never
# committed.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
